0001`) on that commit. It passed.\n- Opened PR #101 against main (https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101) and requested review from `code-owner`.\n\n**What's blocking the merge**\n- PR #101 shows no approvals. Merging into main needs a code-owner approval under policy, so I did not call `merge_pr`.\n- The code-owner reviewer handle I used is `code-owner`, which is the approver name in the policy. If your team uses a specific GitHub user or team, that reviewer should be swapped in.\n\n**Next steps**\n1. Get a code-owner to approve PR #101.\n2. Once it's approved, I can merge it (or you can merge it directly), and the fix will go out with today's release.", "type": "text"}]}]}